==== Modifications (Edge API / RandallFlare) ====

This tree is a modified version of QuantumNous/new-api, rewritten to run as a
Cloudflare Workers-compatible Worker on RandallFlare (workerd + D1 + KV +
static assets via @bigrandall/rrangler).

Material changes from upstream:

- Runtime: Go/Gin + embedded React replaced by a TypeScript Worker on workerd.
- Storage: MySQL/PostgreSQL/SQLite-via-GORM replaced by D1 (SQLite) + KV.
- Password hashing: Argon2id/bcrypt replaced by Web Crypto PBKDF2-SHA256
  (existing upstream password hashes are not portable). This is documented
  PBKDF2-SHA256, not a fake Argon2 implementation.
- Dashboard access tokens are original-shaped JWTs (HS256, iss=new-api,
  aud=new-api-dashboard, 15-minute TTL). The HttpOnly refresh cookie
  `new_api_refresh` is the original `sid.secret` value (Path=/api/user/auth,
  SameSite=Strict) with rotation and AUTH_REFRESH_RACE. Security proofs are
  original-shaped JWTs (`token_use=security_proof`, 1-minute TTL) sent as
  `X-Security-Proof` and consumed once via hashed auth_flows rows.
- The original QuantumNous/new-api TanStack + Rsbuild frontend is vendored
  under web/ and served as ASSETS (public/ is the production build). It is
  not a compact replacement SPA.
- Channel types that require vendor SDKs or local plugins (in-process JS task
  plugins) are exposed in the catalog and will relay when the channel is
  OpenAI/Anthropic/Gemini compatible or uses HTTP pass-through; otherwise they
  return a structured error. Vertex ADC uses the original HTTP path (RS256 JWT
  + `https://www.googleapis.com/oauth2/v4/token`, no Google SDK). AWS AKSK uses
  the original HTTP path (Bedrock `InvokeModel` / `InvokeModelWithResponseStream`
  + SigV4 service `bedrock`, no AWS SDK). AWS ConvertClaudeRequest rewrites
  `source.type=url` to base64 via original GetBase64Data JSON (`type`, `media_type`,
  `data`, omit empty `url`). Extra-OK: skip gin file-source context cache, Worker
  download proxy, ValidateSSRFProtectedFetchURL, and HEIF `decodeImageConfig`.
  OpenAI chat/Responses ConvertRequest HTTP image, file, input_audio, and
  video_url sources are rewritten to Claude `source.type=base64` /
  Gemini `inlineData` via original `MediaContent.ToFileSource` + GetBase64Data
  (`get file data failed: …` / `get file data from '…' failed: …`). Extra-OK:
  ConvertOpenAIRequest stays sync; URL fetch runs in convertOutbound before
  ConvertRequest. Zhipu v4, Volcengine, Perplexity, Ali, NewAPI, Sub2API, and
  Cloudflare ConvertOpenAIResponsesRequest return the request JSON as-is (no openai.Adaptor
  reasoning-suffix rewrite). Baidu v2 ConvertImageRequest / ConvertAudioRequest /
  ConvertEmbeddingRequest / ConvertRerankRequest / ConvertOpenAIResponsesRequest
  are original `not implemented`. xAI ConvertOpenAIResponsesRequest fills empty `model` from
  UpstreamModelName and does not run openai.Adaptor reasoning-suffix stripping.
  Volcengine TTS uses the original HTTP path
  (`wss://openspeech.bytedance.com/api/v1/tts/ws_binary` binary frames, or
  `{base}/v1/audio/speech` JSON `code` 3000, no Volc SDK). Xunfei SparkDesk uses the original HTTP path
  (gorilla `Dial` handshake timeout 5s, HTTP 101 `Upgrade: websocket` to
  `wss://spark-api.xf-yun.com/{version}/chat`, no gorilla SDK). OpenAI Realtime uses the original HTTP path
  (gorilla `DefaultDialer` 45s, HTTP 101 `Upgrade: websocket`, `https`→`wss`, Azure
  `/openai/realtime?deployment=` + `api-key`, preview-only `openai-beta`, Advanced Custom
  route `https`→`wss` + route auth, OpenaiRealtimeHandler `RealtimeUsage` JSON +
  CountTokenRealtime / PreWssConsumeQuota / PostWssConsumeQuota, no gorilla SDK).
  Cloudflare Workers AI STT uses the original HTTP path (`ConvertAudioRequest` raw
  `file` bytes, GetRequestURL `/client/v4/accounts/{ApiVersion}/ai/run/{model}`,
  cfSTTHandler `{text}` from `{result.text}`, ResponseText2Usage completion tokens).
  Extra-OK: STT prompt tokens skip original `GetAudioDuration`.
  OpenAI-model realtime text tokens use original `EstimateToken` (tiktoken-go is not
  bundled). Dial-first 101 then async usage is extra-OK vs original upgrade-first
  then blocking handler. Stripe/Epay/Creem/Waffo checkout use HTTP APIs
  (no vendor SDK). GetTopUpInfo data keys match original `controller.GetTopUpInfo`
  gin.H (no extra `stripe`/`epay`/`creem`/`waffo`/`quota_per_unit`/`price` fields).
  Distributor empty-channel OpenAI errors use original `ErrorCodeModelNotFound`
  (`model_not_found`, HTTP 503, `type: new_api_error`). Extra-OK: task-plugin and
  Midjourney fallbacks may still surface `no_available_channel`.
  Original `middleware.ModelRequestRateLimit` is off by default (`ModelRequestRateLimitEnabled`).
  When enabled, KV is the Redis path: success-list + token-bucket, `abortWithOpenAiMessage`
  429 Chinese messages with empty `code` (no invented 120/min `rate_limit` + `param`).
  Without KV the gin in-memory path returns empty HTTP 429. Extra-OK: KV get/put is not
  Redis lua-atomic. Default `ModelRequestRateLimitSuccessCount` is original `1000`.
  GET `/api/usage/token` runs original `middleware.TokenAuthReadOnly` then
  `controller.GetTokenUsage`. Missing/invalid/disabled keys use gin JSON
  (`success: false`) with original 3-way i18n (`Token not provided` /
  `Invalid token` / `This token status is unavailable` /
  `Database error, please contact the administrator`). GetTokenUsage
  `{code:true,message:"ok",data:{object:"token_usage",...}}` has no `success`.
  Extra-OK: TokenAuthReadOnly still looks up by hyphen-split key; GetTokenUsage
  then re-reads the Bearer remainder without the channel-pin split.
  io.net model deployments use the original HTTP API (no
  vendor SDK). Original QuantumNous factory task plugins (`plugins/tasks/*/plugin.js`)
  are embedded and listed/routed with original JSON (`source: "factory"`).
  Task-plugin `plugin.js` hooks run through the original jsplugin contract
  (forbidden syntax, host `utils`, Call/CallMember, HookError, dry-run JSON)
  on workerd. This is not Goja/sobek; tight-loop Interrupt is the isolate CPU
  limit.   Native plugin routes run original `PrepareTaskPluginRoute`
  (`native.decode` / `native.render` / `native.error` JSON) before submit
  channel distribution. Native submit uses original RelayTask
  `buildSubmitRequest` / `parseSubmitResponse` / `native.render` JSON
  (public `task_id`, no `clientResponse`, `X-New-Api-Other-Ratios`).
  Native query uses original `buildQueryRequest` / `parseTaskResult` /
  `updateVideoSingleTask` JSON (`queryContext` without `requestBody`, public
  `task_id` in `native.render`, persisted `result_url` / `plugin_state`).
  `/v1/videos/:task_id` retrieve uses original `ConvertToOpenAIVideo`
  (`protocols.openai_video.render` + host-owned id/status/progress/model).
  Original `controller.processChannelError` uses `service.ShouldDisableChannel`
  (`channel:` codes, default disable range `401`, AutomaticDisableKeywords;
  not status≥500). Failed attempts set `other_info.status_reason` /
  `status_time` and `abilities.enabled=0`. `ERROR_LOG_ENABLED` RecordErrorLog
  other JSON is public `request_path` / `error_type` / `error_code` /
  `status_code` plus admin `use_channel` (no top-level `channel_id` /
  `channel_name` / `channel_type`). Extra-OK: keyword match is lowercase
  substring, not Aho-Corasick; error-log IP is empty unless RecordIpLog.
  Original `controller.testChannelForHealthCheck` uses ShouldDisableChannel
  plus response-time `channel:response_time_exceeded` (408) when
  AutomaticDisableChannelEnabled and wall time exceeds ChannelDisableThreshold
  (`0` means an impossible 10000000ms). ShouldEnableChannel requires
  AutomaticEnableChannelEnabled (default false) and status auto-disabled.
  Midjourney code 3 uses original UpdateChannelStatus status 2 and
  `No available account instance`. Extra-OK: worker testChannel is a local
  HTTP tester, not the full gin Relay helper; disable uses mapped attempt
  errors; empty OpenAI `error.code` stays `bad_response_status_code`.
  Original `controller.RetrieveModel` looks up only `openAIModelsMap`
  (HTTP 200 `model_not_found` with `param:"model"` when missing, even if
  the model is enabled on a channel) and returns the static catalog row
  with `supported_endpoint_types: null`. Gemini `ListModels` uses original
  `dto.GeminiModel` zero-value JSON (`baseModelId` / `supportedGenerationMethods`
  / etc. null, `nextPageToken: null`). Extra-OK: OpenAI `ListModels` still
  fills `supported_endpoint_types` from the pricing cache (`[]` until
  GetPricing, not null).   Original `controller.ChannelListModels` returns the
  static UniqBy-first catalog with `supported_endpoint_types: null` (not
  pricing-cache or channel-type endpoint arrays). Original
  `controller.GetSubscription` / `GetUsage` use token remain/used/expired and
  unlimited `100000000` only when `DisplayTokenStatEnabled`; otherwise user
  quota/`used_quota` and `access_until: 0`. Extra-OK: gin billing JSON has no
  Cache-Control; worker `json()` still sends `no-store`. Original `model.Channel`
  JSON omits commented-out `MaxInputTokens` (`max_input_tokens` is not a
  Channel field). Original `billing_setting.builtinBillingExpr` includes
  `gpt-image-2` / `gpt-image-2.5-sunburst` / `gpt-image-2.5-flare` /
  `gpt-6-astra`; GetRatioConfig and GetOptions expose those via
  GetBillingModeCopy / GetBillingExprCopy. Original
  `service.BuildTieredTokenParams` + `billingexpr.ComputeTieredQuota` settle
  those exprs (image quota `4113` with ImageTokens/CachedTokensDetails;
  gpt-6-astra standard `7500` / boundary `510000` / long-context `1007510`)
  and `InjectTieredBillingInfo` public log JSON (`billing_mode`, `expr_b64`,
  `billing_tokens`, `image_cache_tokens`, `matched_tier`, `billing_unit`).
  Original `service.GenerateTextOtherInfo` text-relay consume-log JSON always
  includes `model_ratio`, `group_ratio`, `completion_ratio`, `cache_tokens`
  (including `0`), `cache_ratio`, `model_price` (`-1` when ratio-billed),
